PRIVATELY INCIDENT INTAKE =E2=80=94 BACKFILL 4 NEW INCIDENTS

*PRIV-INC-MACSYNC-2026-09 =E2=80=94 CONFIRMED_MALICIOUS_CODE =E2=80=94 Evid=
ence B.*
Kaspersky disclosed a newly observed September 2026 MacSync version on 17
September. The analyzed macOS infection chain delivers an infostealer and
persistent backdoor. Reported targets include saved browser credentials,
wallet-application data, macOS Keychain data, device credentials and
SSH/ZSH configuration. The backdoor can remotely deploy modified browser
add-ons and replace the legitimate Ledger application with a malicious
clone. No established aggregate crypto loss was disclosed.

*PRIV-INC-DCENT-APP-2026-09 =E2=80=94 SUSPICIOUS_UNVERIFIED =E2=80=94 Evide=
nce C.*
D=E2=80=99CENT/IoTrust publicly reported abnormal asset transfers involving=
 its App
Wallet on 16 September and opened an investigation. Public reporting
limited the observed issue to the software App Wallet and did not confirm
an impact originating from D=E2=80=99CENT hardware wallets. Independent XRP=
L
analysis reported a large sweep, but ledger movement alone was not accepted
as proof that those wallets were compromised through D=E2=80=99CENT. Root c=
ause and
accepted loss remained UNKNOWN.
MATERIAL UPDATES

No material upgrade to Needle was recorded.
REJECTED / DUPLICATE CLAIMS

Vite credential-harvesting reporting was treated as older activity rather
than a new hourly incident. Older Mastra, ChainDrop/Shai-Hulud and related
npm incidents were suppressed as historical/duplicate cases.
TOP CASES FOR DEEP FORENSICS

PRIV-INC-DCENT-APP-2026-09 =E2=86=92 wallet/signer investigator: establish =
the
compromise mechanism and whether independent ledger observations can be
technically connected to the provider incident.

PRIV-INC-MACSYNC-2026-09 =E2=86=92 endpoint/key-authority investigator: est=
ablish
which wallet applications/extensions were demonstrably compromised and
whether collected authority produced confirmed drains.
